<title>UNITED NATIONS: Following is ranking of countries on UN index.</title>
<headline>Following is ranking of countries on UN index.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top ranking countries according to the 1997 Human Development Report. The figures used are from 1994 and include life expectancy, education and per capita income according to real gross domestic product for industrial and developing countries. The numbers apply to their overall ranking among all nations:</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL NATIONS:</p>
<p>1. Canada</p>
<p>2. France</p>
<p>3. Norway</p>
<p>4. United States</p>
<p>5. Iceland</p>
<p>6. Netherlands</p>
<p>7. Japan</p>
<p>8. Finland</p>
<p>9, New Zealand</p>
<p>10. Sweden</p>
<p>11. Spain</p>
<p>12. Austria</p>
<p>13. Belgium</p>
<p>13. Australia</p>
<p>15. Britain</p>
<p>16. Switzerland</p>
<p>17. Ireland</p>
<p>18. Denmark</p>
<p>19. Germany</p>
<p>20. Greece</p>
<p>21. Italy</p>
<p>23. Israel</p>
<p>------------</p>
<p>DEVELOPING COUNTRIES (numbers designate overall ranking):</p>
<p>22. Hong Kong</p>
<p>24. Cyprus</p>
<p>25. Barbados</p>
<p>26. Singapore</p>
<p>28. Bahamas</p>
<p>29. Antigua and Barbuda</p>
<p>30. Chile</p>
<p>32. South Korea</p>
<p>33. Costa Rica</p>
<p>36. Argentina</p>
<p>37. Uruguay</p>
<p>38. Brunei Darussalem</p>
<p>40. Trinidad and Tobago</p>
<p>41. Dominica</p>
<p>43. Bahrain</p>
<p>44. United Arab Emirates</p>
<p>45. Panama</p>
<p>46. Fiji</p>
<p>47. Venezuela</p>
<p>49. St Kitts and Nevis</p>
<p>-------------------------------</p>
<p>Top 20 countries when equality for women is measured:</p>
<p>1. Norway</p>
<p>2. Sweden</p>
<p>3. Denmark</p>
<p>4. Finland</p>
<p>5. New Zealand</p>
<p>6. Canada</p>
<p>7. United States</p>
<p>8. Austria</p>
<p>9. Germany</p>
<p>10. Netherlands</p>
<p>11. Australia</p>
<p>12. Switzerland</p>
<p>13. Luxembourg</p>
<p>14. Barbados</p>
<p>15. Belgium</p>
<p>16. Italy</p>
<p>17. Trinidad and Tobago</p>
<p>18. Portugal</p>
<p>19. Bahamas</p>
<p>20. Britain</p>
</text>
